.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected. The feature makes sense to me.\r\n\r\nHowever, there's an issue if you try using this with very thin models (e.g. QuadMesh or PlaneMesh). The Bounding Box mode will create a 0.0-units-thick shape that won't collide with anything else when using Jolt. We can avoid this by ensuring each dimension of the bounding box is at least `0.001` units thick (same for cylinders). This issue doesn't occur in GodotPhysics3D.\r\n\r\n**Edit:** I've reported this in a dedicated issue: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101521#pullrequestreview-2565910898","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101521","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-01-21T23:48:34Z"},{"id":2573780749,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6ZaMcN","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?u=f0c85fe8c24debe91dc14d7efa97b51a19250b47&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","login":"kitbdev","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101521#pullrequestreview-2573780749","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101521","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-01-24T23:25:58Z"},{"id":2573982463,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6Za9r_","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T0